  "guide": {"focus":"The platform and paddle follow paths defined by elapsed time. Forces do not change those paths.","predict":{"prompt":"Will stronger gravity change either driven path?","options":["Neither path changes","Only the platform changes","Both paths change"]},"variables":[{"control":"world.gravity.strength","label":"Gravity strength"}],"steps":[{"text":"Run once and use the limit markers to trace the harmonic and circular paths."},{"text":"Increase gravity, press R, and run the same interval again.","control":"world.gravity.strength"},{"text":"Press R again and check that both objects restart at the same point in their cycles."}],"expect":"Driven positions are functions of elapsed time, so changing gravity does not alter their paths or timing.","limits":"Driven bodies can push other objects through contact. The resulting reaction forces do not alter their prescribed paths."},
